# Asset and Branding Strategy

Rules for asset folders, naming, branding, icons, splash screens, and image quality.

## Requirements

- Asset file names must be lowercase with underscores.
- Must not duplicate the same asset under multiple names.
- Must compress images before committing them.
- Use appropriately sized raster images per context; prefer vectors for simple scalable icons.
- Keep logos in a dedicated folder and register all assets explicitly in `pubspec.yaml`.
- Brand colors must come through the theme system, not raw widget colors.
- Use localized alt text and semantic labels for meaningful images.

## Implementation

- Recommended folders: `assets/images`, `assets/icons`, `assets/logos`, `assets/illustrations`, and `assets/fonts` when needed.
- Keep launcher icon and splash setup documented and repeatable.
- Provide light/dark variants only when the design requires them.

## Acceptance

- Assets load on all supported platforms.
- Large images are not committed uncompressed.
- Reused asset paths are centralized.

